---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/usgaap/asc942.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Loan Origination Fees and Costs — Deferral and Yield Amortization" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Allowance for Credit Losses — Cross-Reference to ASC 326" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Loan Modifications — Post-ASU 2022-02" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Core Deposit Intangibles" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Worked Example — Loan Origination Fee Deferral" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — a Loan Modification Assessment" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. ASC 942 vs IFRS — Comparison" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Related Topics" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Lending economics require yield-based, not fee-based, income recognition</div><div class="principle">Banks, thrifts, and credit unions earn much of their income through the SPREAD between what they pay depositors and what they earn on loans — a genuinely YIELD-based economic model. ASC 942 provides industry-specific guidance ensuring loan origination fees/costs and credit losses are recognised in a way that reflects this underlying ECONOMIC yield, rather than being recognised as isolated, one-off fee transactions.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Banks, savings institutions, and credit unions</div><div class="principle">ASC 942 applies to depository and lending institutions — commercial banks, savings and loan associations, and credit unions.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Loan Origination Fees and Costs — Deferral and Yield Amortization</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Netted against the loan balance, amortised as a yield adjustment</div><div class="principle">Loan ORIGINATION fees received (and DIRECT origination costs incurred) are NOT recognised immediately as revenue/expense — instead, they are DEFERRED, netted against the loan's carrying amount, and AMORTISED over the loan's life as an adjustment to the loan's EFFECTIVE YIELD (generally using the effective interest method) — reflecting that these fees/costs are, in substance, an adjustment to the loan's overall pricing/yield rather than standalone fee income or expense.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Allowance for Credit Losses — Cross-Reference to ASC 326</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The CECL model, applied at industry scale</div><div class="principle">Depository institutions apply the GENERAL Current Expected Credit Loss (CECL) model under ASC 326 to estimate their allowance for credit losses on loan portfolios — a LIFETIME expected loss estimate recognised at ORIGINATION, updated each period. Given the SCALE and CENTRALITY of lending to these institutions' business models, CECL implementation is a particularly significant, resource-intensive undertaking for this industry specifically, even though the underlying MODEL itself is the same general framework applicable to all entities.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Loan Modifications — Post-ASU 2022-02</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The "troubled debt restructuring" (TDR) concept was eliminated for most entities</div><div class="principle">ASU 2022-02 ELIMINATED the separate "troubled debt restructuring" (TDR) recognition and measurement framework that PREVIOUSLY applied when a lender granted a concession to a borrower experiencing financial difficulty. Under CURRENT guidance, such modifications are evaluated under the SAME general loan modification/refinancing framework applied to all loan modifications — with ENHANCED DISCLOSURE requirements specifically for modifications made to borrowers experiencing financial difficulty (e.g. payment deferrals, term extensions, interest rate reductions), rather than a separate TDR accounting model.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Core Deposit Intangibles</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A recognised intangible asset in bank acquisitions</div><div class="principle">In a BUSINESS COMBINATION involving a depository institution, the ACQUIRER often recognises a separate "CORE DEPOSIT INTANGIBLE" asset — representing the value of the STABLE, low-cost deposit base acquired (since core deposits are generally cheaper funding than wholesale borrowing) — amortised over its estimated useful life, consistent with general ASC 805/350 intangible asset recognition principles applied to this industry-specific asset type.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Loan Origination Fee Deferral</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising the fee as a yield adjustment, not immediate income</div>
    <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A mortgage loan origination fee</div><div class="wk-body">A bank originates a $300,000, 30-year mortgage loan, charging a $3,000 origination fee and incurring $1,200 of direct origination costs.</div><div class="wk-answer">The NET fee ($3,000 − $1,200 = $1,800) is DEFERRED and AMORTISED over the loan's life as an adjustment to the EFFECTIVE YIELD — rather than recognised as immediate fee income — resulting in a slightly HIGHER effective interest rate recognised over the loan's term than the loan's STATED interest rate alone would suggest.</div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — a Loan Modification Assessment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Post-ASU 2022-02 disclosure-focused treatment</div>
    <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A payment deferral for a financially distressed borrower</div><div class="wk-body">A bank grants a 6-month payment deferral to a commercial borrower experiencing temporary financial difficulty, without a separate TDR designation under current guidance.</div><div class="wk-answer">The modification is evaluated under the GENERAL loan modification framework (assessing whether it represents a new loan or a continuation of the existing loan) — since the borrower is experiencing financial difficulty, the bank provides ENHANCED DISCLOSURE about the nature and extent of this modification (payment deferral terms, financial effect), consistent with ASU 2022-02's disclosure-focused replacement of the old TDR accounting model.</div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 942 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Loan portfolio composition and credit quality indicators</span><span>Modifications made to borrowers experiencing financial difficulty, including the type and financial effect</span><span>Core deposit intangible balances and amortisation</span></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
    <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a loan modification represents a new loan or a continuation of the existing loan</span><span>Whether a borrower is experiencing financial difficulty, triggering enhanced modification disclosure</span></div></div>
    <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>CECL allowance for credit losses across loan portfolios</span><span>Useful life of core deposit intangibles</span></div></div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>ASC 942 vs IFRS — Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASC 942 vs general IFRS 9 principles</div>
    <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">US GAAP (ASC 942)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IFRS 9)</span></div>
    <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Loan fee/cost deferral</span><span>Deferred, amortised as a yield adjustment</span><span>Same effective interest method principle — converged</span></div>
    <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Credit loss model</span><span>CECL — lifetime expected loss at origination (ASC 326)</span><span>Expected Credit Loss (ECL) — a staged model (12-month vs lifetime depending on credit deterioration), a genuinely different structural approach — see the companion ASC 326 poster</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="note">Loan fee/cost mechanics are broadly converged; the credit loss MODEL divergence (CECL vs IFRS 9's staged ECL) is the more consequential difference, addressed in full in the ASC 326 poster.</div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every ASC 942 event lands</div>
    <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
    <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Loan origination fee/cost</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Deferred, amortised as a yield adjustment over the loan's life</span></div>
    <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Core deposit intangible</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised in a business combination, amortised over its useful life</span></div>
    </div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
    <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
    <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 326</span><span>Supplies the CECL framework for the allowance for credit losses</span></div>
    <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 805</span><span>Governs recognition of core deposit intangibles in bank business combinations</span></div>
    </div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
    <div class="card cn span2">
    <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Core deposit intangible</div><div class="glossary-def">An intangible asset recognised in a bank acquisition representing the value of a stable, low-cost acquired deposit base.</div></div>
    <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Troubled debt restructuring (TDR) — legacy term</div><div class="glossary-def">A concession granted to a financially distressed borrower, formerly subject to special accounting, now addressed through enhanced disclosure under general modification guidance post-ASU 2022-02.</div></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asc942 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
